content+=callout('A tree that leaves room for correction',p('The three infant siblings remembered by Minnie are not individually named or dated. The other older Milstein siblings—Moshe the shochet, David and Liba Malka—remain testimony-based leads. Slot’s remembered daughter is still unidentified. A missing or dashed link is an honest gap, not evidence that a relationship did not exist.','minnie1','minnie2','mark'))
content+=section('Mark Milstein’s 2013 family tree',p('Mark Milstein, Ben’s son, compiled <em>Our Family — 7 generations and counting</em> for Benny’s 90th birthday in May 2013. Mark Cohen supplied this copy. The wide-format chart follows the Milstein and Lederer family, the Gilinsky connections, and Lily Sher’s family, with descendants recorded as of 2013.','mark-milstein-tree')+'<figure><a href="assets/documents/mark-milstein-family-tree-2013.pdf"><img src="assets/images/mark-milstein-family-tree-2013.jpg" alt="Overview of Mark Milstein’s seven-generation family tree, prepared in May 2013" loading="lazy" width="2400" height="480"></a><figcaption><a href="assets/documents/mark-milstein-family-tree-2013.pdf">Open the original PDF and zoom in to read the names and dates</a>.</figcaption></figure>'+p('The chart adds family dates such as Riva and Max’s marriage on 25 December 1938 in Johannesburg, Ben’s birth on 1 May 1923 and Philip’s birth on 4 August 1927. These remain attributed family-history entries. Its 2013 snapshot does not establish anyone’s present living status, and agreement with another family compilation is not necessarily independent confirmation.','mark-milstein-tree'),id='mark-milstein-tree')
page('tree.html','Family tree',content)
# Places and journeys: a schematic, not an invented geographic basemap.
content=head('Place &amp; movement / A family atlas','Different journeys.<br>Connected lives.','A schematic route chart shows the documented sequence without inventing exact routes or stop lengths. Other journeys remain oral history until manifests are found.')
content+='<section class="route-section"><div class="route-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Doba &amp; the three children · 1934</p><h2>From Opalin to Johannesburg</h2></div><ol class="route"><li><strong>Opalin</strong><span>Home in the passport</span></li><li><strong>Warsaw</strong><span>Visa, 21 August</span></li><li><strong>Germany</strong><span>Transit / border stamps</span></li><li><strong>London</strong><span>Departure, 13 September</span></li><li><strong>Cape Town</strong><span>Manifest destination</span></li><li><strong>Johannesburg</strong><span>Train inland, testimony</span></li></ol>'+cite('passport','visa','transit','exit','manifest','riva-id','ben2')+'<p class="caption">Schematic sequence, not a map to scale. The identification card gives 7 October 1934 for Gloucester Castle; it does not map every stop.</p></section>'
places=[('Opalin / Vyshnivka','Family home; today Volyn, Ukraine. The Yahad profile identifies the former town. Do not merge with Ruda Opalin in Poland.',['passport','yahad']),('Warsaw','Mendel’s bakery appears at Ogrodowa 24 in 1928. Doba’s settlement and transit visas were issued here.',['directory','visa','transit']),('Zbąszyń','The Polish exit stamp gives 6 September 1934. It is a border-control locator, not a full rail itinerary.',['exit']),('London','The manifest records embarkation here on 13 September 1934. The tapes recall a shelter and hospitality but do not securely identify the address.',['manifest','opalin1']),('Cape Town & Germiston','Cape Town was the family’s contracted landing port. Ben recalls Moshe meeting the train at Germiston on the way to Johannesburg.',['manifest','ben2']),('Troyeville / Mayfair / Greenside / Emmarentia','The candidate Morris death and Mina marriage share 31 Bezuidenhout Street, Troyeville. Later neighbourhood moves come from testimony; Doba’s estate notice gives 36 Umgeni Road, Emmarentia.',['morris','mina-marriage','ben2','doba-estate']),('Bulawayo','Harry moved in November 1937 in Hela’s account; Hela and Phyllis followed in June 1938. Scott Street and Glen Eagles belong to their story.',['hela2','hela1']),('Dorohusk / Maciejow','Chaya Dwora’s prewar and wartime places in her testimony. Israel Alter’s memoir is in the Dorohusk memorial-book section.',['chaya','alter-memoir']),('Tel Aviv / Palestine','Israel describes arrival in Palestine in 1936. The Film Archive places Naftali’s birth in Tel Aviv in 1947; Mark visited Israel there in 1986.',['alter-memoir','naftali-bio','mark']),('Denver / Buenos Aires','Separate collateral leads: Hela’s maternal aunt Emma in Denver; an unnamed Lederer son associated with Buenos Aires. Neither is a verified household here.',['hela2','opalin1','minnie2']),('Wulka / Volka','The Appelbaum village is only an uncertain sound in the recording. No coordinates or modern identity are assigned.',['minnie2'])]
