# Research questions and conflicts
content=head('The research / What remains open','A place for<br>unanswered questions.','The purpose of this archive is to preserve the evidence and make the next research step specific. It is not to make every gap disappear.')
content+=section('Gilinsky research',p('The <a href="gilinsky.html#next-research">Gilinsky branch</a> tracks Solomon’s estate TAB MHG 6258/56, Edith’s estate 1336/56, the Leah identification, Station Jewellers and unidentified children in family photographs. Solomon’s archive enquiry was sent on 20 November 2026; no estate packet has been received.','gil-estate','gil-edie-gazette','gil-mark'))
questions=[('Emma in Denver','Identify Hela’s mother’s sister, tentatively Emma Ray. Look for a husband working in coal delivery and records naming her parents. Do not assume a Lederer maiden name.',['hela2'],'Next focused lead'),('Moshe and Arke’s voyages','Find their separate passenger lists before Doba’s September 1934 departure. Search Moshe/Moishe/Moses/Morris and Milstein/Millstein/Milsztejn variants; Stillman and Kirshner may help.',['minnie1','ben1'],'Unlocated'),('The Morris–Moshe identification','The certificate fits the operation, timing, place and household address. A named spouse, parent or linked estate is still needed.',['morris','mina-marriage'],'Strong candidate'),('Doba’s estate','Obtain full packet 2783/77. The Gazette notice is now downloaded and visually checked, but the FamilySearch range remains digitally restricted. Enquiry sent; reply awaited.',['doba-estate','doba-film'],'Awaiting archive reply'),('Isaac’s estate and Slot children','Obtain TAB MHG 5056/52 and the Doba marriage record. Resolve Nick/Leslie and Hayme/Hymie/Helman, and identify the remembered sister.',['isaac-estate','annie','ethan'],'Awaiting archive reply'),('Arke’s residence and dates','Find Aron’s death notice or estate to identify an address. Kensington and Selwyn Segal are compatible leads, not proof. Do not search Krugersdorp solely because of the parcel-trip explanation.',['aron-grave','selwyn','mark'],'No personal care file'),('Nutke’s formal identity','A spouse, approximate birth year or clearer portrait inscription could distinguish him from same-name victims. Do not merge the Appelbaum uncle.',['nutke-photo','minnie1','minnie2'],'Unresolved'),('Mendel’s two testimonies','Reconcile 1880/baker/Warsaw ghetto with 1885/merchant/Treblinka. Identify Doba Kam and Menukha Il without assuming either is a known relative. Name the Argentina son.',['mendel-a','mendel-b','directory'],'Conflicting accounts'),('Hela’s mother and sisters','Confirm Yosefa as Hela’s mother, Freida as her sister and Chuma as the possible Nechama. A clear recording review or civil record would help.',['hela2','yosefa','freida','chuma'],'Strong / partial matches'),('The older Opalin generations','Check current custody and availability of the 1858 revision lists and 1860–1861 material before ordering. The guide entries are not named family records.',['guide1858','guide1860'],'Archive leads'),('Surviving family papers','Locate Doba’s letters to Hela and Minnie, Riva’s schoolwork and maps, and the grandfather’s photograph remembered as held in Israel.',['hela1','minnie1','opalin1'],'Family collection leads'),('Alter relationship','A clear human review of Minnie’s aunt-name and an explicit full-name relationship record would strengthen the older sibling link. Preserve the memoir/interview chronology discrepancies.',['minnie1','alter-memoir','naftali-interview','chaya'],'Strong converging case')]
